MISDA PROJECT FILE STRUCTURE
================================================================================

1. CORE LIBRARY
---------------

misda/__init__.py
    Small public facade exporting the static MISDA API:
      - discover: structural inference and complete MIS universe.
      - evaluate: candidate-level linear, nonlinear, Pareto, and dominance evidence.
      - rank: ranking views under named policies.
      - benchmark: declaration-aware scientific assessment kept outside discovery.

misda/api.py
    Static discovery/evaluation/ranking implementation and typed result model:
      - MISSet and MISCandidate.
      - Ranking and named ranking policies.
      - StructuralMetrics, LinearMetrics, NonlinearMetrics, ParetoMetrics, and
        DominanceMetrics.
      - DimensionalSupport, CandidateSupport, and reduction assessment.

misda/_reporting.py
    Rich, side-effect-free stored-state reporting for discovery, ranking,
    candidate evidence, support diagnostics, and selected reductions.

misda/_graph.py
    Construction of G+ and G±, independence-number dimensions, and structural
    MIS enumeration.

misda/_statistics.py
    Correlation statistics, alpha_onset/alpha_null estimation, empirical null
    envelope calibration, and aggressiveness interpolation.

misda/_support.py
    Data-driven dimensional-support diagnostics:
      - TRANSITIVE_CHAINING.
      - HIDDEN_SPECTRAL_STRUCTURE.

misda/_reconstruction.py
    Linear and nonlinear external reconstruction engines and nonlinear null
    reference protocol.

misda/_pareto.py
    Empirical Pareto-front preservation metrics.

misda/_dominance.py
    Observed pairwise dominance-preservation evidence used by the experimental
    dominance_preservation ranking policy.

misda/_ranking.py
    Structural candidate measurements used by ranking policies.

misda/_plotting.py
    Matplotlib structural-graph rendering over already discovered graph state.

misda/_front_plotting.py
    Ranking-aware compatibility selection plus intrinsic MIS-level interactive
    Plotly Pareto-front views, including notebook display and terminal/browser
    HTML fallback.

misda/benchmark.py
    Benchmark declarations, reports, serialization, and regression comparison.

misda/benchmarks/
    Controlled diagnostic problem definitions, truth helpers, reproducible
    classical references, comparison helpers, and validation infrastructure.

misda/benchmarks/validation.py
    Shared implementation for fixed-noise controlled validation, clean
    multi-sample robustness, and observation-noise robustness.


2. BENCHMARK NOTEBOOKS & FRONT ENDS (benchmarks/)
--------------------------------------------------

benchmarks/controlled.ipynb
    Canonical 13-case controlled benchmark under exact observation Y=Z.

benchmarks/controlled_noisy.ipynb
    The same 13-case benchmark under a fixed scale-relative noisy observation
    regime.

benchmarks/sampling_robustness.ipynb
    Clean sampling study across independent sample seeds with sigma=0.

benchmarks/noisy_robustness.ipynb
    Focused multi-sigma/multi-replicate observation-noise robustness study.

benchmarks/comparison.ipynb
    MISDA/PCA comparison on clean controlled diagnostics with explicit truth.

benchmarks/classical.ipynb
    Reproducible DTLZ reference problems; analytical front geometry is reference
    context, not MISDA latent/structural truth.

benchmarks/optimization.ipynb
    Paired optimization proof-of-concept comparing Full and Reduced problems in
    the original objective space.

benchmarks/run_controlled.py
benchmarks/run_controlled_noisy.py
benchmarks/run_sampling_robustness.py
benchmarks/run_noisy_robustness.py
benchmarks/run_comparison.py
benchmarks/run_classical.py
    Executable front ends corresponding to the benchmark batteries above.

benchmarks/run_ranking_policy_impact.py
    Reproducible pre-default audit comparing size_span and
    dominance_preservation on identical generated objective matrices.

benchmarks/run_ranking_policy_aggressiveness_probe.py
    Manual policy-by-aggressiveness follow-up used to distinguish threshold
    sensitivity from noisy representative-selection sensitivity.


3. DOCUMENTATION
----------------

docs/userguide.md
    User-facing guide for the current static API and benchmark workflow.

docs/visualization.md
    User-facing visualization contract and examples.

docs/experimental-correlation.md
    Reproducible documentation for the explicitly gated Spearman research
    backend; the canonical default remains Pearson.

docs/CONTRIBUTING.md
    Contribution guidance, including public-capability preservation rules.

docs/adr/
    The single normative architectural and methodological ledger. ADRs define
    the current method and public-contract invariants.

docs/research-notes/
    The chronological MISDA research notebook: hypotheses, experiments,
    negative results, corrections, validation evidence, and open questions.
    It is scientific provenance, not normative specification.
